# NOTE - If this is a shared desktop and each user has their own musica
# database, they SHOULD install a copy in their OWN user space so as not
# to impact other users' access to their content.

# Master User - This is a single/multiple user(s) who have the ability to 
# not only query a db, but also to edit/add/delete records from the db.
# Depending on the enviornment, there can be one, multiple or no Master Users.
# The Notes application checks the logged in user against the Master User 
# list to determine what privileges the current user has. 
#
# MASTER_USER is simply the name of the logged in user. If the user 
# attempting to access Notes is on the MASTER_USER list, they have access 
# to full editing capabilities and can add/delete/edit/query a record. If
# the user IS NOT on the MASTER_USER list, they can only query the db.
#
# To set the MASTER_USER, replace the string <user_id> with the users
# account name. If more than one user is to be granted MASTER_USER status, 
# Add a new line with the users system id. For example:
# MASTER_USER=<user_id-1>
# MASTER_USER=<user_id-2>
